// Checked integer arithmetic contract (Rust `overflow-checks = true` semantics).
//
// Consumed here (not invented in a backend): every `*WithOverflow` MIR rvalue
// expands to the matching `num.sal` macro below (`EXPAND NUM_*_CHECKED`), and
// the value it computes is exact — overflow traps with `panic(9001)` instead
// of wrapping, which is what rustc's overflow `Assert` enforces.
//
// The three `@extern` decls below are legacy (mir2sars no longer emits calls
// to them); they stay for link-compat only. New lowering must use the macros.
@extern sa_num_add_checked(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64
@extern sa_num_sub_checked(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64
@extern sa_num_mul_checked(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64
